// Two questions a client asks about a card's sides, and they are not
// the same question. `BACK_IMAGE` is whether Scryfall serves a second
// picture for the printing this pool pinned, read off `image_uris` —
// which Scryfall puts at exactly one of two levels, on the card for one
// piece of cardboard and on each face for two. `DOUBLE_FACED` is
// CR 712.1: a card with a face on each side and no Magic card back,
// in three kinds — nonmodal, modal, and meld.
//
// They differ, and the difference is why there are two tables: a meld
// card is double-faced and has no back image, because Scryfall models
// a meld back as a card of its own rather than as a face. Neither is
// `faces.len() > 1`, which is a count of what this build compiled and
// is the bug this table replaces (#115).
